{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-730fdace-62fa-44dd-9263-fc7c492131c4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a1d6143b9bb0079","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-76z2k0yq/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E003.md","content":"# Konflux build pipeline for the vLLM ROCm serving runtime image\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic onboards the vLLM ROCm runtime image build to Konflux so the new image variant is built, validated, and released through the platform's standard pipeline, like the existing CUDA runtime images. The midstream vLLM repo is already Konflux-onboarded; this epic adds the pipeline/application configuration for the ROCm image variant. This is known-recipe onboarding work that is needed for any go outcome of the validation campaign and proceeds in parallel with the campaign and with the runtime productization work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add Konflux application/pipeline configuration for the vLLM ROCm image variant in the already-onboarded midstream vLLM repo.\n- Wire the image build, including the ROCm base image inputs, into the existing release automation so the ROCm variant is produced per platform version.\n- Ensure pipeline outputs (images, provenance) are visible to the release process used for the serving runtime.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A Konflux pipeline builds the vLLM ROCm image variant from the midstream repo and completes green.\n- The pipeline is wired into the release automation so the ROCm image variant is produced as part of a platform version build.\n- The pipeline run records the ROCm base image inputs used for the build.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)** (enabling): A supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime is productized for the cleared models — this epic provides the build/release infrastructure that productization requires. It carries no DAG dependency on the productization work: the two run in parallel, with the pipeline-green condition expressed as an acceptance criterion on the productization epic.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The ROCm base image inputs track AMD's upstream release cadence (open question 2); the pipeline must tolerate base-image updates between platform versions.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":37591,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cd51f53f58a6d98","agent_id":"ae6b38f613648449c","session_id":"ca871b20-94d5-42d0-a66d-2838b98e5410","uuid":"73737a1b-d983-46a6-a9c1-effbf35b3fb0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:25:36.446Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
