{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-239bc0bc-992a-4bb1-968d-4135d316d0d8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-81e75d3160bd04ec","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-76z2k0yq/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E004.md","content":"# PyTorch ROCm training support for PyTorchJob single- and multi-GPU jobs\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers PyTorch training on ROCm for jobs run through the Training Operator: ROCm-enabled PyTorch training runtime images and the PyTorchJob configuration needed to run single-GPU and multi-GPU (including multi-node) training jobs on AMD Instinct nodes. It provides the training half of the AMD enablement independent of the serving validation outcome — training support proceeds on the strength of upstream PyTorch ROCm support and is validated directly on the hardware.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build/enable the ROCm variant of the PyTorch training runtime image used by PyTorchJob workers.\n- Verify PyTorchJob single-GPU and multi-GPU job topologies run on AMD Instinct nodes with the ROCm training runtime.\n- Verify multi-node jobs are admitted and run through the platform's workload queueing when enabled (gang admission of the job's pods).\n- Validate functional training correctness (loss convergence / job completion) for representative training workloads on ROCm.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A PyTorchJob using the ROCm training runtime completes successfully on AMD Instinct hardware in single-GPU configuration.\n- A PyTorchJob using the ROCm training runtime completes successfully in multi-GPU configuration on AMD Instinct hardware.\n- A multi-node PyTorchJob is admitted through a Kueue queue configured for the `amd.com/gpu` resource and runs to completion (end-to-end admission check; the quota configuration itself is delivered by the Distributed Workloads quota-handling work and consumed here as a configuration reference).\n- Job results demonstrate training correctness (jobs complete without ROCm-related failures) for the tested workloads.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling. This epic delivers the training-runtime and PyTorchJob half of HLR-3; the quota-handling half is delivered by the Distributed Workloads epic.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Validation requires access to dedicated AMD Instinct nodes — the same availability precondition as the serving validation campaign (procurement/partner lab, unresolved). Job validation is scheduled around whatever access window is secured.\n- Upstream PyTorch/ROCm release cadence (open question 2) may limit which ROCm versions can be validated per platform release.\n- The mechanism that exposes the `amd.com/gpu` resource on nodes (AMD GPU device plugin/operator) is not part of the platform inventory and is not addressed by the strategy; this epic assumes it is present on the target clusters. Flagged in the decomposition summary for human verification.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":38186,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cd51f53f58a6d98","agent_id":"ae6b38f613648449c","session_id":"ca871b20-94d5-42d0-a66d-2838b98e5410","uuid":"6a5146a0-fb83-49e7-80b5-1ac30c956b8e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:25:47.062Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
