{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0f5e9449-d98b-4155-bd15-a9d62b4ab4a7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-95d6a0da852376f5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-76z2k0yq/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E005.md","content":"# Kueue quota handling for the amd.com/gpu resource\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers quota handling for the `amd.com/gpu` resource in the platform's Kueue-based queueing layer, so workloads requesting AMD GPUs are accounted, quota-gated, and admitted with the same all-or-nothing semantics as NVIDIA GPU workloads. It covers the resource-flavor and cluster-queue configuration surface in the Distributed Workloads stack that makes `amd.com/gpu` a quota-managed resource.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the ResourceFlavor covering nodes that expose the `amd.com/gpu` resource.\n- Provide the ClusterQueue/LocalQueue configuration pattern for `amd.com/gpu` quota, mirroring the existing NVIDIA GPU quota handling.\n- Verify quota accounting: workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted only when quota is available, and pending/admitted accounting is correct.\n- Verify gang semantics: multi-pod workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted all-or-nothing (waitForPodsReady behavior).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A workload requesting `amd.com/gpu` is admitted by a ClusterQueue configured with the AMD resource flavor when quota is available, and remains pending when it is not.\n- Quota accounting for `amd.com/gpu` matches admitted usage (no over-admission beyond configured quota).\n- A multi-pod workload requesting `amd.com/gpu` is admitted all-or-nothing — partial pod sets are not scheduled when full quota is unavailable.\n- The configuration is documented sufficiently for cluster administrators to deploy AMD GPU quota for their queues.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling. This epic delivers the amd.com/gpu quota-handling half of HLR-3; the training-runtime half is delivered by the Training Operator epic. The two run in parallel — training jobs consume the quota configuration as a configuration reference (acceptance-criterion gate), not as a build dependency.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The `amd.com/gpu` resource must be exposed on nodes by an AMD GPU device plugin/operator that is not in the platform inventory and is not addressed by the strategy; this epic configures quota against the resource name and assumes exposure exists on target clusters. Flagged in the decomposition summary for human verification — if the exposure mechanism must be productized, an additional epic is needed.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":38952,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cd51f53f58a6d98","agent_id":"ae6b38f613648449c","session_id":"ca871b20-94d5-42d0-a66d-2838b98e5410","uuid":"386e707d-ebf3-413d-8fb1-1d014105765c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:25:56.974Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
