on covers both serving runtime usage and PyTorchJob training usage, including `amd.com/gpu` quota configuration for administrators.\n- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented behavior of the serving runtime, training runtime, and quota handling (reviewed by the owning engineers, not just editorially).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-4 (P2)**: Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list. This epic is the full delivery of HLR-4. Its priority is P1 per the docs-authoring exception (strategy priority Major → P1), and it is blocked by all implementation epics per the docs-last rule.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Content depends on the validated model list and driver details finalized by the implementation work; authoring starts only after those are complete.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39661,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cd51f53f58a6d98","agent_id":"ae6b38f613648449c","session_id":"ca871b20-94d5-42d0-a66d-2838b98e5410","uuid":"d84b09df-4873-406d-82dc-aab8a234d264","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:26:08.221Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020 into epics"}
