{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8be44778ff644307","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n3\ttitle: PyTorch ROCm training support for PyTorchJob single- and multi-GPU jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: -1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PyTorch ROCm training support for PyTorchJob single- and multi-GPU jobs\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers PyTorch training on ROCm for jobs run through the Training Operator: ROCm-enabled PyTorch training runtime images and the PyTorchJob configuration needed to run single-GPU and multi-GPU (including multi-node) training jobs on AMD Instinct nodes. It provides the training half of the AMD enablement independent of the serving validation outcome — training support proceeds on the strength of upstream PyTorch ROCm support and is validated directly on the hardware.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Build/enable the ROCm variant of the PyTorch training runtime image used by PyTorchJob workers.\n38\t- Verify PyTorchJob single-GPU and multi-GPU job topologies run on AMD Instinct nodes with the ROCm training runtime.\n39\t- Verify multi-node jobs are admitted and run through the platform's workload queueing when enabled (gang admission of the job's pods).\n40\t- Validate functional training correctness (loss convergence / job completion) for representative training workloads on ROCm.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- A PyTorchJob using the ROCm training runtime completes successfully on AMD Instinct hardware in single-GPU configuration.\n45\t- A PyTorchJob using the ROCm training runtime completes successfully in multi-GPU configuration on AMD Instinct hardware.\n46\t- A multi-node PyTorchJob is admitted through a Kueue queue configured for the `amd.com/gpu` resource and runs to completion (end-to-end admission check; the quota configuration itself is delivered by the Distributed Workloads quota-handling work and consumed here as a configuration reference).\n47\t- Job results demonstrate training correctness (jobs complete without ROCm-related failures) for the tested workloads.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling. This epic delivers the training-runtime and PyTorchJob half of HLR-3; the quota-handling half is delivered by the Distributed Workloads epic.\n52\t\n53\t## Risks / Notes\n54\t\n55\t- Validation requires access to dedicated AMD Instinct nodes — the same availability precondition as the serving validation campaign (procurement/partner lab, unresolved). Job validation is scheduled around whatever access window is secured.\n56\t- Upstream PyTorch/ROCm release cadence (open question 2) may limit which ROCm versions can be validated per platform release.\n57\t- The mechanism that exposes the `amd.com/gpu` resource on nodes (AMD GPU device plugin/operator) is not part of the platform inventory and is not addressed by the strategy; this epic assumes it is present on the target clusters. Flagged in the decomposition summary for human verification.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88f49970e427ed12","agent_id":"a233ed0a79fbe8521","session_id":"ca871b20-94d5-42d0-a66d-2838b98e5410","uuid":"9a3b989d-2a23-4fa2-b701-470231d4bc46","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:28:32.826Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8be44778ff644307","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
