{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae8db996c9ed524b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E005\n3\ttitle: Kueue quota handling for the amd.com/gpu resource\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue quota handling for the amd.com/gpu resource\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers quota handling for the `amd.com/gpu` resource in the platform's Kueue-based queueing layer, so workloads requesting AMD GPUs are accounted, quota-gated, and admitted with the same all-or-nothing semantics as NVIDIA GPU workloads. It covers the resource-flavor and cluster-queue configuration surface in the Distributed Workloads stack that makes `amd.com/gpu` a quota-managed resource.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Define the ResourceFlavor covering nodes that expose the `amd.com/gpu` resource.\n38\t- Provide the ClusterQueue/LocalQueue configuration pattern for `amd.com/gpu` quota, mirroring the existing NVIDIA GPU quota handling.\n39\t- Verify quota accounting: workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted only when quota is available, and pending/admitted accounting is correct.\n40\t- Verify gang semantics: multi-pod workloads requesting `amd.com/gpu` are admitted all-or-nothing (waitForPodsReady behavior).\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- A workload requesting `amd.com/gpu` is admitted by a ClusterQueue configured with the AMD resource flavor when quota is available, and remains pending when it is not.\n45\t- Quota accounting for `amd.com/gpu` matches admitted usage (no over-admission beyond configured quota).\n46\t- A multi-pod workload requesting `amd.com/gpu` is admitted all-or-nothing — partial pod sets are not scheduled when full quota is unavailable.\n47\t- The configuration is documented sufficiently for cluster administrators to deploy AMD GPU quota for their queues.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: PyTorch training on ROCm is supported for single- and multi-GPU jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling. This epic delivers the amd.com/gpu quota-handling half of HLR-3; the training-runtime half is delivered by the Training Operator epic. The two run in parallel — training jobs consume the quota configuration as a configuration reference (acceptance-criterion gate), not as a build dependency.\n52\t\n53\t## Risks / Notes\n54\t\n55\t- The `amd.com/gpu` resource must be exposed on nodes by an AMD GPU device plugin/operator that is not in the platform inventory and is not addressed by the strategy; this epic configures quota against the resource name and assumes exposure exists on target clusters. Flagged in the decomposition summary for human verification — if the exposure mechanism must be productized, an additional epic is needed.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88f49970e427ed12","agent_id":"a233ed0a79fbe8521","session_id":"ca871b20-94d5-42d0-a66d-2838b98e5410","uuid":"64e6f025-b85b-4909-80d5-ff493ad80fca","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:28:33.581Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae8db996c9ed524b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
