raining on ROCm: how to run single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJob training on AMD nodes, including Kueue quota configuration for `amd.com/gpu`.\n47\t- The validated model list: models cleared by the validation campaign, with the functional/performance parity findings summarized.\n48\t- Support boundaries: what is unsupported (GPU sharing/partitioning, non-AMD accelerator families per the strategy's out-of-scope list).\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Published documentation states the supported AMD Instinct hardware and the driver prerequisites for serving and training.\n53\t- Published documentation states the validated model list, matching the go/no-go scope produced by the validation campaign.\n54\t- Published documentation covers both serving runtime usage and PyTorchJob training usage, including `amd.com/gpu` quota configuration for administrators.\n55\t- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented behavior of the serving runtime, training runtime, and quota handling (reviewed by the owning engineers, not just editorially).\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- **HLR-4 (P2)**: Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list. This epic is the full delivery of HLR-4. Its priority is P1 per the docs-authoring exception (strategy priority Major → P1), and it is blocked by all implementation epics per the docs-last rule.\n60\t\n61\t## Risks / Notes\n62\t\n63\t- Content depends on the validated model list and driver details finalized by the implementation work; authoring starts only after those are complete.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab379a7fba01f9c7","agent_id":"a71994d836a7933eb","session_id":"ca871b20-94d5-42d0-a66d-2838b98e5410","uuid":"23c173d5-25c4-4a66-a9a4-17a5ebb6774a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:31:37.575Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a31d374f61e8f4ce","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_ty