{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-899c25605bf77737","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E006\n3\ttitle: Document AMD hardware support, driver prerequisites, and validated models\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Documentation\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E003\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E004\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9020-E005\n14\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n15\tai_signals:\n16\t  change_specificity: 1\n17\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n18\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n19\t  existing_foundation: 1\n20\t  open_questions: 0\n21\t  external_dependency: 0\n22\t  human_process_gates: -1\n23\t  repo_access: 1\n24\t  architecture_claims: 0\n25\tinvestigation_signals: null\n26\tai_implementability: High\n27\tai_implementability_score: 3\n28\tjira_key: null\n29\tbranch: null\n30\tgated_by: null\n31\tgate_failure_impact: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Document AMD hardware support, driver prerequisites, and validated models\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tThis epic delivers the customer-facing documentation for AMD GPU (ROCm) enablement: the supported AMD hardware, the driver prerequisites for running serving and training workloads on AMD Instinct accelerators, and the validated model list produced by the validation campaign. It is authored through the Red Hat docs content process once the implementation work it describes is final.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\tContent outline:\n42\t\n43\t- Supported AMD hardware: the AMD Instinct accelerators on which serving and training are supported.\n44\t- Driver and cluster prerequisites: AMD driver versions and node requirements, including how the `amd.com/gpu` resource must be exposed on nodes.\n45\t- Serving on ROCm: how to deploy the vLLM ROCm serving runtime for the validated models, including model-scope limitations from the validation campaign.\n46\t- Training on ROCm: how to run single- and multi-GPU PyTorchJob training on AMD nodes, including Kueue quota configuration for `amd.com/gpu`.\n47\t- The validated model list: models cleared by the validation campaign, with the functional/performance parity findings summarized.\n48\t- Support boundaries: what is unsupported (GPU sharing/partitioning, non-AMD accelerator families per the strategy's out-of-scope list).\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Published documentation states the supported AMD Instinct hardware and the driver prerequisites for serving and training.\n53\t- Published documentation states the validated model list, matching the go/no-go scope produced by the validation campaign.\n54\t- Published documentation covers both serving runtime usage and PyTorchJob training usage, including `amd.com/gpu` quota configuration for administrators.\n55\t- The content is technically reviewed against the implemented behavior of the serving runtime, training runtime, and quota handling (reviewed by the owning engineers, not just editorially).\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- **HLR-4 (P2)**: Documentation states supported AMD hardware, driver prerequisites, and the validated model list. This epic is the full delivery of HLR-4. Its priority is P1 (strategy priority Major → P1), and it is blocked by all implementation epics because the documentation is authored after the behavior it describes is final.\n60\t\n61\t## Risks / Notes\n62\t\n63\t- Content depends on the validated model list and driver details finalized by the implementation work; authoring starts only after those are complete.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b874be8fc0f9242c","agent_id":"a89a7279af9598f38","session_id":"ca871b20-94d5-42d0-a66d-2838b98e5410","uuid":"d8ca3172-55a3-4505-adf4-71d4c4e27d85","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:32:50.752Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-899c25605bf77737","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type"